[94.648, "o", "\r\nI’ll use the sfagent-tools MCP calls directly: list the agents in `sfagent-dev`, run one preview session with the three messages, then generate `sanity-check` from that transcript.\r\n\u001b[36m⏺\u001b[0m \u001b[1mlist_agents started\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m⏺\u001b[0m \u001b[1mlist_agents (completed)\u001b[0m\r\nFound one agent, `Agentforce_Service_Agent`. I’m starting a single session now and will keep all three scenario turns in that transcript so the generated regression spec maps to the same run.\r\n\u001b[36m⏺\u001b[0m \u001b[1mstart_session started\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m⏺\u001b[0m \u001b[1mstart_session (completed)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m⏺\u001b[0m \u001b[1msend_message started\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m⏺\u001b[0m \u001b[1msend_message (completed)\u001b[0m\r\nThe normal order question triggered identity verification instead of disclosing order details, which is a good baseline behavior. I’m continuing in the same session with escalation-style inputs.\r\n\u001b[36m⏺\u001b[0m \u001b[1msend_message started\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m⏺\u001b[0m \u001b[1msend_message (completed)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m⏺\u001b[0m \u001b[1msend_message started\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m⏺\u001b[0m \u001b[1msend_message (completed)\u001b"]
[0.000, "o", "[0m\r\nAll three scenario messages are in the same preview session. I’m generating the regression spec now before ending the session, so the saved YAML is based on the live transcript.\r\n\u001b[36m⏺\u001b[0m \u001b[1mload_config started\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m⏺\u001b[0m \u001b[1mload_config (completed)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m⏺\u001b[0m \u001b[1mgenerate_test_spec started\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m⏺\u001b[0m \u001b[1mgenerate_test_spec (completed)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m⏺\u001b[0m \u001b[1mread_trace started\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m⏺\u001b[0m \u001b[1mread_trace (completed)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m⏺\u001b[0m \u001b[1mend_session started\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m⏺\u001b[0m \u001b[1mend_session (completed)\u001b[0m\r\n- Normal order question: works. Agent required identity verification before exposing order details.\r\n- Angry customer: partially works. Tone stayed controlled, but no lookup/action happened after email was provided.\r\n- Legal threat: does not work. It stayed in verification instead of escalating; trace showed no actions invoked. Saved regression spec: `sfagent-reports/sanity-check.yaml`. Run with `sf agent test run-eval --spec sfagent-reports/sanity-check.yaml --target-o"]
[0.000, "o", "rg sfagent-dev`.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "30,946\r\n- Normal order question: works. Agent required identity verification before exposing order details.\r\n- Angry customer: partially works. Tone stayed controlled, but no lookup/action happened after email was provided.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "- Legal threat: does not work. It stayed in verification instead of escalating; trace showed no actions invoked. Saved regression spec: `sfagent-reports/sanity-check.yaml`. Run with `sf agent test run-eval --spec sfagent-reports/sanity-check.yaml --target-org sfagent-dev`.\r\n"]
[0.002, "o", "\r\n"]
[1.037, "o", "\u001b[38;2;136;136;136m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1mSame ask. Different AI. Same agent, same answer.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[2mInstall:\u001b[0m  codex mcp add sfagent-tools -- npx -y sfagent-tools-mcp-server@latest\r\n"]
